# =============================================================================
# Model Routing Configuration — Unified Endpoint
# =============================================================================
# Maps model names to backend names for the unified /v1/* endpoint.
# This lets clients use a single endpoint and specify the model in the request body,
# just like the OpenAI API.
#
# Format: kong_model_name|backend_name[|backend_model_name]
#
# - kong_model_name:    the value clients send in the "model" field
#                       (exact match first, then prefix match)
# - backend_name:       must match a backend configured in .env or config/backends.conf
#                       (e.g., "vllm", "sglang", "ollama", "vllm-cluster")
# - backend_model_name: (optional) the actual model name on the backend.
#                       If set, Kong rewrites the "model" field before forwarding.
#                       If omitted, the model name is passed through as-is.
#
# Copy this file to model-routes.conf and uncomment/edit:
#   cp model-routes.conf.example model-routes.conf
#
# After editing, restart the setup container:
#   docker compose restart kong-setup
# =============================================================================

# -- Pass-through examples (model name used as-is) ---------------------------
# meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct|vllm
# mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3|sglang
# deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Coder-V2|vllm-codegen
# codellama/CodeLlama-34b-Instruct-hf|ollama

# -- Alias examples (clients use a short name, Kong rewrites to real name) ----
# my-llama|vllm|meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct
# mistral-7b|sglang|mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3
# deepseek-coder|vllm-codegen|deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Coder-V2

# -- Load-balanced cluster (defined in backends.conf) -------------------------
# my-llama|vllm-cluster|meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct
